11:25.530 --> 11:27.290
Class Journal

11:25.530 --> 11:27.290
Class 5-1

11:26.030 --> 11:27.280
Nishimura-san.

11:27.280 --> 11:28.210
Huh?

11:29.120 --> 11:31.860
Um... Adachi-san?

11:32.370 --> 11:33.950
Do you have a moment?

11:38.330 --> 11:42.720
Nishimura-san, you hang out 
a lot with Dai-chan, right?

11:43.150 --> 11:45.930
Dai-chan's birthday is 
right around the corner.

11:45.930 --> 11:49.050
I was wondering what to get as a present...

11:49.050 --> 11:50.390
So, um...

11:50.390 --> 11:54.550
Could you casually ask Dai-chan 
to see what he wants?

11:54.550 --> 11:57.320
Um, who's Dai-chan?

11:57.810 --> 11:58.690
Ah!

11:59.460 --> 12:02.080
B-By Dai-chan, I mean Daichi-kun!

12:02.080 --> 12:03.790
Daichi-kun?

12:06.200 --> 12:07.810
Yo!

12:08.700 --> 12:10.660
<i>Does she mean Hino-kun?</i>

12:12.160 --> 12:13.570
How about it?

12:13.570 --> 12:19.190
Well, I think you should ask Hino-kun 
directly about something like that.

12:19.540 --> 12:22.180
I c-couldn't possibly...

12:22.180 --> 12:23.360
Did you call me?

12:23.360 --> 12:24.110
Huh?

12:28.750 --> 12:31.440
Nice timing. Adachi-san was just—

12:31.440 --> 12:33.280
I-I-It's nothing!

12:33.280 --> 12:34.510
It's nothing, really!

12:34.510 --> 12:36.650
Hey, it's Umi!

12:36.650 --> 12:38.530
Don't see you two together every day.

12:38.530 --> 12:40.470
I-Is that so?

12:40.470 --> 12:42.000
Hold on, Umi.

12:42.000 --> 12:43.890
Your face is bright red.

12:43.890 --> 12:46.230
Maybe you've got a fever.

12:47.870 --> 12:51.520
I... I... I-I-I'm fine!

12:55.620 --> 12:58.020
Look at that! She's sure full of energy.

13:00.040 --> 13:02.330
<i>Wait, does she...</i>

13:10.090 --> 13:13.860
I'm... in love with Dai-chan.

13:15.340 --> 13:18.850
We've been neighbors since we were kids.

13:19.140 --> 13:22.320
So it's not like there was a 
defining moment or anything.

13:23.540 --> 13:27.790
Back in early grade school, we'd run around 
and play, and I thought nothing of it.

13:28.250 --> 13:29.230
But...

13:30.260 --> 13:36.510
the girls around me started caring about 
fashion and forming friend groups...

13:38.860 --> 13:41.560
I realized as we started to grow apart...

13:41.560 --> 13:42.840
that I loved him.

13:43.350 --> 13:46.760
So I'm jealous of you, Nishimura-san.

13:46.760 --> 13:48.380
Huh? Why?

13:48.380 --> 13:51.880
You're so close with boys, like Takada-kun.

13:52.880 --> 13:54.880
<i>That's not it, Adachi-san.</i>

13:54.880 --> 13:58.140
<i>That's just because I don't 
have any other friends.</i>

13:58.530 --> 14:02.170
Does this mean you won't ask him
 about a present for me?

14:02.170 --> 14:03.400
No, I've got it.

14:03.400 --> 14:05.990
I'll ask him casually.

14:05.990 --> 14:07.160
Really?

14:07.160 --> 14:08.390
Thanks!

14:08.390 --> 14:11.060
I'm so glad I asked you, Nishimura-san!

14:11.060 --> 14:11.810
Yeah.

14:13.610 --> 14:16.110
Um, please keep this a secret.

14:16.110 --> 14:17.310
It's embarrassing.

14:17.310 --> 14:19.010
Okay, sure thing.

14:19.010 --> 14:20.430
Ah!

14:21.170 --> 14:24.280
The Grim Reaper and Adachi 
are plotting something!

14:24.280 --> 14:26.330
Adachi's pals with the Grim Reaper!

14:26.330 --> 14:28.170
She was spying on us humans!

14:28.170 --> 14:31.090
N-Nishimura-san is no Grim Reaper...

14:31.090 --> 14:33.510
If that's true, you'd talk in the classroom

14:33.510 --> 14:36.180
instead of behind everyone's backs out here!

14:36.980 --> 14:39.660
There are things you can't 
talk about in the classroom.

14:39.660 --> 14:44.300
You were talking in secret like spies!

14:45.010 --> 14:47.400
<i>Adachi looks uncomfortable.</i>

14:47.400 --> 14:50.300
<i>This is all my fault... What do I do?</i>

14:50.690 --> 14:52.960
Good for you, Grim Reaper!

14:52.960 --> 14:55.130
You've got yourself an obedient minion!

14:55.130 --> 14:56.210
What?!

14:56.210 --> 14:58.290
The Grim Reaper has a minion?!

14:58.290 --> 15:00.200
What's that? It sounds so cool!

15:00.200 --> 15:01.950
Ugh, it's Takada!

15:01.950 --> 15:02.720
Ah!

15:03.200 --> 15:06.790
<i>What? Takada calls her the Grim Reaper, too?</i>

15:07.220 --> 15:08.190
Hey, hey!

15:08.190 --> 15:10.690
I wanna be the Grim Reaper's minion, too!

15:10.690 --> 15:13.560
A-Adachi-san's not really my minion.

15:13.560 --> 15:15.470
What are you doing here, Takada?!

15:15.720 --> 15:17.190
Oh, that's right!

15:17.190 --> 15:21.990
So, this weekend, we're having a 
birthday party for Hino-kun at my place!

15:21.990 --> 15:23.330
It's a surprise party!

15:24.870 --> 15:28.150
I'd love it if you could come, Nishimura-san!

15:28.150 --> 15:29.510
You wouldn't mind?

15:29.510 --> 15:30.670
Of course not!

15:30.670 --> 15:32.870
O-Okay. I'll be there.

15:34.380 --> 15:36.380
What about you guys?

15:36.380 --> 15:38.740
Huh?! Why us?

15:41.080 --> 15:42.300
But, well...

15:42.300 --> 15:45.600
I don't mind showing up if 
the Grim Reaper's not there!

15:45.600 --> 15:48.250
It'll be a snoozefest with her around.

15:50.080 --> 15:52.290
What are you saying, Kitagawa-kun?

15:52.290 --> 15:57.180
Nishimura-san the Grim Reaper
makes every day so much fun!

16:00.570 --> 16:05.180
Without you around, 
I bet life would be so boring.

16:09.250 --> 16:10.450
<i>I see.</i>

16:10.450 --> 16:14.400
<i>Nishimura-san doesn't mind 
when Takada-kun uses her nickname.</i>

16:14.770 --> 16:16.600
Let's get out of here, Kitagawa.

16:16.600 --> 16:18.850
Takada's always like this.

16:18.850 --> 16:20.710
Dang it! Remember this!

16:20.710 --> 16:22.220
Yeah, you bet!

16:24.970 --> 16:27.740
I'll have to write about it in 
my diary so I don't forget.

16:27.740 --> 16:30.110
S-Spare him that at least.

16:31.410 --> 16:34.380
Sorry, Adachi-san, are you okay?

16:34.380 --> 16:36.190
Thanks, I'm fine.

16:36.890 --> 16:39.260
Hey, do you want to join us, as well?

16:39.260 --> 16:41.390
For Hino-kun's surprise party.

16:41.390 --> 16:42.800
W-Would that be okay?

16:43.070 --> 16:44.550
Adachi-san wants in?

16:44.550 --> 16:48.510
I'm sure Hino-kun would be happy 
to have his childhood friend there.

16:48.510 --> 16:50.000
His childhood friend?

16:50.000 --> 16:51.820
Yeah, you could say that.

16:52.220 --> 16:55.070
Then you should definitely come!

16:55.070 --> 16:57.930
Besides, you're friends with Nishimura-san.

16:57.930 --> 16:59.300
You're welcome to join us!

16:59.300 --> 16:59.980
Huh?

17:06.650 --> 17:08.120
Hino-kun!

17:08.120 --> 17:10.830
Happy birthday!

17:10.830 --> 17:13.730
Whoa, what a surprise.

17:15.090 --> 17:17.680
Me and my sister baked this cake!

17:17.680 --> 17:18.910
Try some, try some!

17:18.910 --> 17:21.510
Wow, looks tasty!

17:22.150 --> 17:24.670
Gee, everyone, thanks!

17:33.610 --> 17:34.950
Oh, Umi.

17:35.190 --> 17:37.770
H-Happy birthday, Dai-chan.

17:37.770 --> 17:38.870
Here.

17:38.870 --> 17:40.660
Hey, thanks!

17:40.660 --> 17:41.900
Can I open it?

17:41.900 --> 17:42.960
Y-Yeah.

17:48.090 --> 17:50.140
You look so cool, Hino-kun!

17:50.140 --> 17:51.160
Nice!

17:51.160 --> 17:52.500
Looking good!

17:58.200 --> 17:59.680
Show me, show me!

17:59.680 --> 18:00.930
Thanks.

18:00.930 --> 18:03.160
No, I didn't do anything.

18:03.160 --> 18:05.990
Takada-kun's the one who threw the party.

18:07.770 --> 18:09.800
Hmm? What's wrong?

18:09.800 --> 18:10.960
I'm sorry.

18:10.960 --> 18:12.480
Huh? For what?

18:12.750 --> 18:17.010
Well... you got swept up into 
being treated as my friend.

18:17.010 --> 18:18.800
They might tease you again.

18:18.800 --> 18:20.290
Oh, that's no problem.

18:20.290 --> 18:23.120
I'm sorry I didn't say 
anything back then, either.

18:23.460 --> 18:27.630
I was happy when he said I was your friend.

18:27.630 --> 18:29.860
M-Me, too.

18:29.860 --> 18:31.760
And so, um...

18:32.050 --> 18:35.770
Do you mind if I call you Akane-chan?

18:41.840 --> 18:45.970
In that case... I'll call you...

18:51.920 --> 18:55.090
<i>I-I called her "Umi-chan"!</i>

18:57.500 --> 19:00.400
<i>Something I learned from making friends</i>

19:00.400 --> 19:05.510
<i>is that things can be a little awkward
as you first get to know each other.</i>

20:47.320 --> 20:48.550
Take this!

20:51.230 --> 20:53.770
The magic spear Dark Dancer!

20:54.370 --> 20:55.740
Takada-kun!

20:58.560 --> 21:02.180
Hey, are you and Nishimura-san going out?

21:02.850 --> 21:04.380
If I said we are...

21:05.200 --> 21:07.080
What would that mean?

21:07.760 --> 21:08.700
Come on!

21:08.700 --> 21:11.470
You don't even know that? 
You're such a kid!

21:11.470 --> 21:13.120
I mean, I <i>am</i> a kid.

21:13.120 --> 21:15.510
I'm saying you're being childish right now!

21:15.990 --> 21:17.040
Listen up.

21:17.040 --> 21:22.760
Going out means going
 on dates and kissing and stuff.

21:23.020 --> 21:25.270
We've never done any of that!

21:25.580 --> 21:26.930
Really?

21:26.930 --> 21:28.620
Really!

21:28.620 --> 21:30.390
Is that right?

21:30.390 --> 21:33.770
In that case, you're practically strangers.

21:33.770 --> 21:35.250
What?!

21:35.750 --> 21:40.380
S-Strangers? But I think we 
get along pretty well.

21:41.380 --> 21:44.530
A boy and girl who aren't going 
out might as well be strangers!

21:44.820 --> 21:46.220
N-No way...

21:46.220 --> 21:49.780
I thought that was all grown-up stuff...

21:49.780 --> 21:52.030
That's why I'm saying you're a kid.

21:52.470 --> 21:56.370
Even we go and dates and kiss!

21:56.370 --> 21:58.170
I mean, not me personally.

21:58.530 --> 22:01.180
<i>That's</i> how boys and girls get along!

22:04.310 --> 22:07.470
Good thing Nishimura-san didn't 
beat you to the punch.

22:07.470 --> 22:10.590
Hmph! It's not like I'm relieved or anything!

22:23.390 --> 22:24.730
What's wrong?

22:26.320 --> 22:29.730
Do you see me as a kid, too?

22:29.730 --> 22:31.510
Well, yeah.

22:31.510 --> 22:33.240
We're both kids.

22:34.340 --> 22:35.970
Nishimura-san...

22:35.970 --> 22:38.260
When we grow up, can I kiss you?

22:38.530 --> 22:39.230
What?!

22:39.230 --> 22:41.290
Wh-Where'd that come from?!

22:42.250 --> 22:48.000
Kasahara-san said all that, but I think 
it's still too much for kids..

22:48.500 --> 22:52.010
Sorry, I have no idea what brought this on.

22:58.790 --> 23:00.150
You're right!

23:00.150 --> 23:02.520
The two of us are friends!

23:02.520 --> 23:05.130
Y-Yep, we're friends.

23:05.130 --> 23:06.420
Friends!

23:06.420 --> 23:10.540
I was sad because Kasahara-san
said we were strangers.

23:11.740 --> 23:13.080
You gave me quite a start...

23:13.690 --> 23:14.740
<i>But...</i>

23:23.370 --> 23:25.040
<i>is it normal for a friend...</i>

23:28.420 --> 23:31.250
<i>to make your heart beat so fast?</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next time...</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
<b>Field Trips and the Magic of Marinated Eggs</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
Akane's lunch box
